      "start": 83,
      "end": 111,
      "parent_id": null,
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "structure_method": "text-paragraphs-and-list-markers/2",
      "window_ids": [
        "window-16b20beddb05a62e20ff"
      ],
      "processing": "processed"
    },
    {
      "id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:passage:c3e6a81e77540f341e80727ce7cec9401df36a59196afd2064ff148ac7f4c5aa",
      "source": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:document:2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008",
      "text": "a. The role of the consular officer is now limited to\r\nproviding information obtained from foreign officials on requirements for local\r\nmarriages and performing notarial and authentication services.\n\n",
      "claim_ids": [
        "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:1c83ba7430543c804ec7c99b50b9fe28a6f95e6a90336bb2ce0a26ab430b01de"
      ],
      "evidence_refs": [
        {
          "id": "urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008:111:311:sha256-33234cb8f90fbca3de43ad758a6dc2cc3dbe71e478fb0853dbf6818a3b1131be",
          "roles": [
            "source"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008:111:309:sha256-90372037d467b8c8b97f79569497158fdb8a43155888650a40ea9d0a98ae26b9",
          "roles": [
            "summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "start": 111,
      "end": 311,
      "parent_id": null,
      "kind": "list_item",
      "structure_method": "text-paragraphs-and-list-markers/2",
      "window_ids": [
        "window-16b20beddb05a62e20ff"
      ],
      "processing": "processed"
    },
    {
      "id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:passage:e295c27943fdc4b51e3a3788fb5c62e95930a3182469b5ea60c42c10ad9647af",
      "source": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:document:2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008",
      "text": "b. Prior to November 9, 1989, consular officers, when\r\nrequested to do so, could make certain that foreign marriages were effective\r\nfor purposes of U.S. law by acting as official witnesses to the marriage, when\r\none of the contracting parties was a U.S. citizen, pursuant to the authority of\r\nSection 31 of the Act of June 22, 1860 (12 Stat. 79; 22 U.S.C. 4192). The Act\r\nalso provided for issuance of an official certificate of witness to such\r\nmarriage.\n\n",
      "claim_ids": [
        "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:204d486e4dabc1efea8ab46177c7b46111c98edbd9e8d31785fb869ff0b1ceea"
      ],
      "evidence_refs": [
        {
          "id": "urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008:311:769:sha256-c525998f1e79d9908fbd5efa743724a0a4d86f1e5d6874bc41002f1304e7eaf7",
          "roles": [
            "source"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008:311:767:sha256-559556255c20c0c2c5f303377edf4e5a723139e9847e40c341cd620d09000d19",
          "roles": [
            "summary",
            "scope_text:0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "start": 311,
      "end": 769,
      "parent_id": null,
      "kind": "list_item",
      "structure_method": "text-paragraphs-and-list-markers/2",
      "window_ids": [
        "window-16b20beddb05a62e20ff"
      ],
      "processing": "processed"
    },
    {
      "id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:passage:943ec93762ec6710a13777a8d2729566ac3714cd944bee8f415837db661b39e4",
      "source": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:document:2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008",
      "text": "c.  Section 31 was repealed, effective February 16,\r\n1990, by Section 123 of the FY 1990-1991 Foreign Affairs Authorization Act. \n\n",
      "claim_ids": [
        "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:f59a50c54e9189e20f754fc27be3629b39d9a4fc851a4c48638a9218df207974"
      ],
      "evidence_refs": [
        {
          "id": "urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008:769:900:sha256-363088ea044637a0f2e7a8b394224df594bcda1bf1fdec176197cc07ff5466fc",
          "roles": [
            "source"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3A2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008:769:897:sha256-8fb0cc3c7f8c34f7c999ce9677f5ce46e34e1f5fb6fa639851479abde09ac4b5",
          "roles": [
            "summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "start": 769,
      "end": 900,
      "parent_id": null,
      "kind": "list_item",
      "structure_method": "text-paragraphs-and-list-markers/2",
      "window_ids": [
        "window-16b20beddb05a62e20ff"
      ],
      "processing": "processed"
    },
    {
      "id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:passage:2e4a0adacca8e009aa4ee4b7fd4cc6c166888a21842a0892174fe8014c079f7b",
      "source": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:document:2f1b8c8b8a8e5f20335289c9791b49c29e25931f2eb629b02018723fe3ee8008",
      "text": "d. Certificates of Witness to Marriage, issued by\r\nconsular officers pursuant to Section 31 of the Act of June 22, 1860, prior to\r\nits repeal, remain valid. Such certificates, using the most recent edition of\r\nForm FS-87, were issued from when it was revised in October 1939, until\r\nNovember 9, 1989.\n\n",
      "claim_ids": [
        "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:fe383be002d16ce7c62253d33a8a78aeb5981a40ba6d7f698d622133c26a3b74"
      ],
